      "canonical": [
        {
          "name": "This page treats $L^p(\\mu)$ as a quotient of measurable functions modulo almost-everywhere equality, so pointwise statements on $L^p$ first choose a representative.",
          "disposition": "included",
          "item": "rem-elements-of-l-p-are-equivalence-classes-and-pointwise-statements-require-a-representative"
        },
        {
          "name": "On this page, Riesz-Fischer means completeness of $L^p$ and the subsequence consequence, not the Fourier-coefficient theorem from later harmonic or Hilbert-space pages.",
          "disposition": "included",
          "item": "thm-riesz-fischer-completeness-of-l-p"
        },
        {
          "name": "The range $0 < p < 1$ is deliberately limited to three items: failure of the norm axioms, the complete translation-invariant metric on the quotient, and the reverse inequality for nonnegative functions.",
          "disposition": "included",
          "item": "thm-the-l-p-distance-for-zero-less-p-less-one-is-a-complete-translation-invariant-metric"
        },
        {
          "name": "The Banach-space phrasing is recorded only as an orientation seam; the page's proof-bearing theorem is completeness itself.",
          "disposition": "included",
          "item": "rem-lp-completeness-and-the-banach-property"
        },
        {
          "name": "On a finite counting space, the integral Holder and Cauchy-Schwarz statements are exactly the published finite-dimensional inequalities.",
          "disposition": "included",
          "item": "rem-finite-counting-measure-holder-and-cauchy-schwarz-agree-with-published-finite-inequalities"
        },
        {
          "name": "The equality case in Minkowski is split out from the proof's single Holder step: proportionality of |f| and |g| almost everywhere is the exact criterion.",
          "disposition": "included",
          "item": "thm-equality-case-in-minkowski-inequality"
        },
        {
          "name": "On a finite counting space, the integral Minkowski theorem is exactly the published finite-dimensional Minkowski inequality.",
          "disposition": "included",
          "item": "rem-finite-counting-measure-minkowski-agrees-with-the-published-finite-theorem"
        },
        {
          "name": "Lyapunov interpolation is the exact Holder-powered comparison block from two endpoint L^p norms to every intermediate exponent.",
          "disposition": "included",
          "item": "thm-lyapunov-interpolation-inequality-for-l-p-norms"
        },
        {
          "name": "The Lyapunov item is recorded explicitly as the log-convexity statement for p mapsto log ||f||_p on the interval where the endpoint norms are finite.",
          "disposition": "included",
          "item": "rem-lyapunov-inequality-is-equivalent-to-log-convexity-of-p-to-log-norm"
        },
